    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.Act.app.profiles.import">Import…</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.Help.app.profiles.Intro">A profile is a complete setup: where thumbnails sit, hotkeys, colours, crops and client layout. Keep one per activity, like mining and PvP.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.Help.app.profiles.profiles.Title">Working with profiles</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.Help.app.profiles.profiles.Body">- **New** starts an empty profile and switches to it.&#x0A;- **Copy** copies one profile into another: everything, or only thumbnail positions.&#x0A;- **Delete** removes the current profile for good. You always keep at least one.&#x0A;&#x0A;You can also switch from the profile menu at the top left, or with the profile hotkeys.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.Help.app.profiles.backups.Title">Backups and moving to another PC</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.Help.app.profiles.backups.Body">**Back up now** saves a dated copy in the Backups folder next to MultiPreview.&#x0A;&#x0A;**Export** saves your settings file wherever you like. **Import** replaces all your settings with an exported file. Your current settings are backed up first, and MultiPreview needs a restart to use the imported ones everywhere.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.Page.app.about">About &amp; updates</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.Page.app.about.Desc">Version, updates and the old settings window.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.Sec.app.about.version">MultiPreview</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.app.about.versionText">EVE MultiPreview {0}</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.app.about.links">Updates and source code</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.Act.app.about.checkNow">Check for updates</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.Act.app.about.github">Open the GitHub page</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.Sec.app.about.updates">Updates</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.app.about.checkOnStartup">Check for updates when MultiPreview starts</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.app.about.preRelease">Get pre-release builds</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.app.about.preRelease.Desc">Try new features early. Pre-releases can have more bugs.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.app.about.installVersion">Install a specific version</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.app.about.installVersion.Desc">Any release, older or newer. Going back to an older one turns off the startup update check.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.Act.app.about.install">Install</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.Sec.app.about.window">Settings window</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.app.about.useOldWindow">Use the old settings window</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.app.about.useOldWindow.Desc">Go back to the previous settings window. It will be removed in a later release.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.app.about.useOldWindow.Toast">Done. The settings window you picked opens the next time you open settings.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.About.Checking">Checking for updates…</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.About.UpToDate">You're up to date ({0}).</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.About.CheckFailed">Couldn't check for updates: {0}</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.Help.app.about.Intro">Check for updates, try pre-releases, install any version, or go back to the old settings window.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.Help.app.about.updates.Title">Updates</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.Help.app.about.updates.Body">MultiPreview checks GitHub for a new release when it starts, unless you turn that off. **Check for updates** checks right now.&#x0A;&#x0A;**Install a specific version** lists every release. Installing an older one turns off the startup check, so it doesn't offer to update straight back.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.Help.app.about.window.Title">The old settings window</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.Help.app.about.window.Body">The previous settings window stays available while the new one settles in. Turn on **Use the old settings window**, then reopen settings to use it. In the old window, **Try the new settings window** brings you back.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.Old.TryNewWindow">Try the new settings window (preview). Takes effect the next time you open settings.</sys:String>
</ResourceDictionary>
